        <li><b>25+</b><span>Years in technology</span></li>
        <li><b>200+</b><span>Clients served</span></li>
        <li><b>Rakuten</b><span>Technology exit</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="cover-cap"><b>Reggie James</b><span>Founder, Digital Clarity</span><span>COO and Executive Director, DBMM Group Inc. (OTC: DBMM)</span></p>
</header>

<section class="band why" id="why" aria-labelledby="why-h">
  <div class="wrap why-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Why work with me</p>
      <h2 class="h-sec" id="why-h">Advice is easy to find. Experience is harder to buy.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="why-copy">
      <p>I have spent much of my career on the other side of the table: building businesses, managing people, winning and losing customers, investing in new ideas, and making decisions when there isn't an obvious answer.</p>
      <p>I understand what it is like to carry responsibility for a business. And I know that the right strategy means very little unless someone can make it work.</p>
      <p>I bring that experience to the leaders I advise: independent thinking, commercial perspective and a willingness to get involved.</p>
      <ul class="why-facts">
        <li>Founded Digital Clarity in 2002 and grew it to more than 200 clients</li>
        <li>Built DC Storm through to its acquisition by Rakuten</li>
        <li>Led commercial operations for an internet business listed in Singapore</li>
        <li>COO and Executive Director of a US public company since 2011</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band dark asks" id="questions-leaders" aria-labelledby="asks-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="pe-head">
      <h2 class="h-sec" id="asks-h">The questions leaders bring me</h2>
      <p>These are leadership questions. They need someone who understands the whole business, not just one function.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="ask-list">
      <li>Why aren't we growing as quickly as we should?</li>
      <li>Are we investing in the right things?</li>
      <li>Is our proposition strong enough to win?</li>
      <li>Do we have the right people and commercial structure?</li>
      <li>Should we enter a new market, change direction or acquire a business?</li>
      <li>What needs to change to make this company more valuable?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band services" id="services" aria-labelledby="svc-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="pe-head">
      <h2 class="h-sec" id="svc-h">How I work with leaders</h2>
      <p>Four ways to work together, each built around a situation leaders face rather than a list of functions.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="svc-grid">
      <article class="svc">
        <h3>The CEO's Commercial Adviser</h3>
        <p class="for">For founders and CEOs who want an experienced, independent voice alongside them.</p>
        <p>Working directly with you on growth decisions, commercial priorities, market positioning, investment and execution. A trusted outside perspective, with the experience to challenge assumptions and help management make better choices.</p>
        <p class="eng"><span>How it works</span>Monthly advisory, with regular leadership sessions and access between meetings.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="svc">
        <h3>The Growth and Performance Review</h3>
        <p class="for">For businesses investing in growth but not getting the returns they expect.</p>
        <p>An independent look at the commercial model: customers, proposition, pipeline, pricing, market opportunity, people and execution. A clear answer to what is working, what isn't and what management should do next.</p>
        <p class="eng"><span>How it works</span>Fixed-fee diagnostic and board-level recommendations, with optional support to implement them.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="svc">
        <h3>The Investor's Commercial Partner</h3>
        <p class="for">For investors who want to know whether a business can deliver its commercial ambitions.</p>
        <p>Pre-investment commercial assessment, proposition and market reviews, post-investment growth priorities, and hands-on support for portfolio leadership teams.</p>
        <p class="eng"><span>How it works</span>Deal-specific review, portfolio advisory or ongoing commercial involvement.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="svc">
        <h3>The Next Chapter</h3>
        <p class="for">For a business that needs to change direction.</p>
        <p>Entering a new market, developing a new proposition, commercialising technology, adapting to AI-driven change or preparing for a new phase of growth. Helping leadership define the opportunity, make the commercial decisions and put a workable plan in place.</p>
        <p class="eng"><span>How it works</span>Strategic project, with optional fractional executive involvement.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <a class="pill dark-pill" href="#contact">Talk through which fits</a>
  </div>
</section>

